.TH MAPT 1 "September 2026" "mapt 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mapt \- two panel package manager for APT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mapt
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mapt
is a two panel, full screen terminal interface for APT written in C with
ncurses.  The left panel lists the packages reported as installed by
.BR dpkg-query (1)
(optionally only those with an upgrade available),
the right panel lists the packages of the APT cache that are not
installed, together with their candidate version and origin repository:
the two panels are a strict partition of the database.
.PP
Packages with dependencies (Depends or PreDepends) show a "[+]" marker
left of their name; expanding the tree inserts their direct
dependencies as indented child rows, drawn in cyan when the child
is installed itself.
.PP
Reading data never requires root privileges.  Every command that changes
the system is run through
.B sudo
and only after an explicit confirmation dialog.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.SS Panels
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Home ", " End
Move the cursor.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch the focused panel.  A mouse click in either panel has the same
effect.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Left ", " Right
Expand or collapse the dependency tree of the current package
(Right expands, Left collapses, Enter toggles).
.TP
.B F3
Show details of the selected package.
.TP
.BR F4
List the files owned by the package (dpkg \-L), or the archive file.
.TP
.BR F7
Find a package by substring.
.TP
.IR a\-z ", " Backspace ", " Esc
Incremental (jump to) search inside a panel.
.SS Mouse
.TP
.B Left click
Activate a panel and select the package under the pointer.  Double click
expands or collapses its dependency tree.
.TP
.B Wheel
Scroll either panel, text viewers and live command output.
.TP
.B Click
Invoke menu titles, menu entries, function-key labels, dialog buttons and
scrollbar tracks.  In a text field, click to place the cursor.
.SS Marking and actions
.TP
.B Insert
Toggle the mark of the current package and move down.
.TP
.B +
Mark packages matching a glob pattern.
.TP
.B \-
Clear all marks in the current panel.
.TP
.B F5
Install (or reinstall) the marked or selected packages.
.TP
.B F6
Upgrade the marked or selected packages.
.TP
.BR F8 ", " Delete
Remove the marked or selected packages.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Re-read the package database.
.SS Global
.TP
.BR F1 ", " F2 ", " F9 ", " F10
Help, menu, menu, quit.
.SH PROGRESS
When the package tools report percentages (apt-get run with
\-\-show\-progress, or dpkg's "Reading database ... NN%" lines) the
command window draws a progress bar; such lines are shown as the bar
only and never appear in the log.  When no percentage is available
(for example during
.BR "apt-get update" )
an animated spinner is drawn instead.  The startup window that loads
the package database shows the spinner next to the current step as
well.
.SH FILES
No configuration files are used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR apt-cache (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
APPIT Adam Skowroński <info@appit.pl>.
